Crime Scenario Summary:
Title: Employee Fired for Theft and Corporate Espionage
Overview: Jake Fosters was a senior employee at ABC Technologies, a company specializing in high-tech software solutions. After working there for over 8 years, Jake was unexpectedly fired for alleged misconduct related to internal theft and corporate espionage. The company alleges that Jake has been stealing proprietary information, including company software code and client data, and selling it to competitors for financial gain. This theft and betrayal have caused significant financial damage to ABC Technologies, and now, investigators need to gather digital evidence to uncover the extent of the wrongdoing.
The investigation is centered around John's actions leading up to his termination. John was accessing confidential files, deleting records, and using his personal devices to store and transmit company data. The flash drive provided contains a variety of evidence related to this crime, and it is crucial to search and analyze all the items stored on it for any incriminating data.
